<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Takelot III</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">8th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Takelot III was an Egyptian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">pharaoh</a> of the 8th century BCE, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osorkon-iii">Osorkon III</a>, who first served as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/high-priest-of-amun">High Priest of Amun</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thebes">Thebes</a> and then as co-ruler with his father. He belonged to the line of kings based at Thebes and Herakleopolis often called the Twenty-third Dynasty, in a period when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> was split among rival rulers before the Kushite conquest.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/takelot-iii.jpg" alt="Takelot III" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Neithsabes · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karnak_Takelot_III.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
